Coimmunoprecipitation
Double homozygous Arabidopsis lines expressing GmACBP4.1:EGFP and GmACBP4.2:EGFP with DsRed:VLXB were identified after genetic crosses. Roots were harvested from 4-week-old plants with/without 150 mM NaCl treatment for CoIP, as described previously (
Lung et al., 2017
). Briefly, 25 μL of Affi-Gel 10 beads (Bio-Rad) which had been coupled with anti-ACBP3 antibodies were incubated with 250 μL of 1 mg mL
−1
crude protein extracts at 4°C for 1 h on a rotary shaker. The beads were washed thrice and eluted with 50 μL of elution buffer containing 0.1 M glycine-HCl (pH 2.4) and 0.15 M NaCl. The proteins were neutralized with 10 μL of 1 M Tris–HCl (pH 8), and analyzed by immunoblotting using anti-ACBP3 and anti-DsRed (1:2,000; Takara; catalog no. 632496) antibodies.
Salt tolerance test of soybean hairy roots
GmACBP4.1
and
GmACBP4.2
ORFs were amplified using primers ML3293/ML3129 and ML3293/ML3165, and cloned into the
Xho
I site of pCambia3301 (CAMBIA; replacing
bar
